# Worms Armageddon: Anniversary Edition (PPSA20052): reach a fixed-map playable Training level.
# Seconds are measured from the first pad poll. One-second holds are poll-safe.
#
# Why this route exists alongside reach-gameplay.pad: Quickstart generates its terrain RANDOMLY per
# run. Two independent fresh-save runs of reach-gameplay.pad produced a pirate/treasure map and a
# fairytale/castle map, and frames from the second scored at most 0.6567 SSIM against references
# built from the first, against a 0.85 floor -- so no fixed-reference content guard can be built on
# that route. Training levels are authored fixed maps. Under this route two independent runs matched
# at 0.9612-1.0000, so it is the route the snapshot guard uses. reach-gameplay.pad remains the route
# for the published Quickstart-match milestone.
#
# Observed on a Linux hardware-Vulkan boot at scale 4 (480x270), consistent across two runs:
#   ~8-13 s   Digital Eclipse studio splash
#   ~14 s     title screen ("PRESS X TO START GAME"), 75,875 distinct colours
#   21-26 s   main menu after the first Cross ("PLAY THE GAME")
#   27-32 s   game-setup grid after the second Cross; 3 columns x 2 rows, Quickstart preselected
#             top-left, Single Player directly below it -- hence one Down rather than any Right
#   33-38 s   Single Player selected in the grid
#   39-62 s   Single Player screen, Training tab active, focus on the tab row; the three Downs walk
#             focus out of the tab row and down the right-hand column to the Start button
#   63-70 s   "Grenade skills grade 1" mission brief prompt
#   ~72 s     the training level is loaded and playable; its 60-second mission timer expires ~132 s
# The Crosses at 78 and 86 land in the level and are harmless; they cover brief-prompt timing
# variation without changing the level that loads.
20-21:cross
26-27:cross
32-33:down
38-39:cross
44-45:down
50-51:down
56-57:down
62-63:cross
70-71:cross
78-79:cross
86-87:cross
